## General Python conventions

- Type-hint function signatures where it adds clarity. Skip type hints for trivial helpers.
- Prefer explicit imports (`from x import y`) over wildcard imports (`from x import *`).
- Run tests before committing. Don't commit code that fails the existing test suite.
- Keep functions focused. If a function does more than one thing, split it.

